  "description": "## How we proceed ?\n\n1. We create a simple feature in the [_Script_](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/a7QE8ig7/script/) tab.\n2. In order to capture the relevant patterns explaining the churn, we tested three common algorithms -- Random Forrest, Logistic Regression and Gradient Boosting Trees. See [here](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/a7QE8ig7/ml/p/mHAYEcNw/settings/) for all available options for training.\n\n\n## Assessing models\n\n1. Once training is complete, the trained models that are available in the [_Models_](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/a7QE8ig7/ml/p/mHAYEcNw/) tab with their scores and a small display on the most important hints for each model type.\n\n2. You have more details on each model. Take a look for example at the [coefficients](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/a7QE8ig7/ml/p/mHAYEcNw/A-DKU_CHURN-a7QE8ig7-mHAYEcNw-s14-pp3-m1/report/#coefficients) of the linear model and [variables importance](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/a7QE8ig7/ml/p/mHAYEcNw/A-DKU_CHURN-a7QE8ig7-mHAYEcNw-s14-pp1-m1/report/#variables_importance) of the random forest model.\n\n3. You can also create [charts](/projects/DKU_CHURN/analysis/a7QE8ig7/ml/p/mHAYEcNw/A-DKU_CHURN-a7QE8ig7-mHAYEcNw-s14-pp1-m1/charts/) on the validation set of a model.\n\n## Deployment\n\nThe best model (RANDOM FOREST) have been deployed in the [flow](/projects/DKU_CHURN/flow/) and is used to compute a churn likeliness score on each customer.",
